Credits

The driver speaks the panel's local JSON interface as PIMA's "Force Interface
JSON Format Specification" v2.4 describes it, and the panel's standard alarm
reports (SIA DC-09 with Contact-ID or SIA codes) for panels without it.

How the panel behaves in the field (framing, ACKs, the account, Windows-1255
text, pacing) was checked against these projects:

- C4-PimaForce (https://github.com/efic1/C4-PimaForce), MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2026 Efi.
- pima-force-ha-integration (https://github.com/amithalp/pima-force-ha-integration),
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Assaf Arbelle (@aarbelle) and amithalp.
  The panel frames in tests/test_force_protocol.lua are taken from its test
  fixtures (the account and names there are synthetic).
- homebridge-pima-force (https://github.com/electricmonk/homebridge-pima-force),
  LGPL-3.0, read for protocol facts only; none of its code is included.

