src/x25519.lua and src/base64.lua come from DirectorLink
(https://github.com/DirectorLink/DirectorLink, Apache License 2.0, Copyright
2026 DirectorLink). x25519.lua follows TweetNaCl's field arithmetic
(https://tweetnacl.cr.yp.to/, public domain). The tests' aes.lua and sha256.lua
come from DirectorLink's tests as well, and tests/alarm_command.json is
DirectorLink's shared test vector.

Control4 interfaces follow the public Snap One DriverWorks documentation
(https://snap-one.github.io/docs-driverworks-fundamentals/) and Snap One's
security proxy template code
(https://github.com/snap-one/drivers-template-code-public).

The SIA DC-09 reports in tests/test_sia.lua were captured from a FORCE 32C
(firmware 1.5.1). The account in them is a made-up number set for the test,
and they hold no codes or names.
